llocated_memory_after_bytes": 20454995968, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 20454989312, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the following information:\n\n- **Normal sleep time**:  \n  Kim usually goes to sleep at **10 p.m.** and wakes up at **6 a.m.**, so her usual sleep duration is:\n  $$\n  6:00 \\text{ a.m.} - 10:00 \\text{ p.m.} = 8 \\text{ hours} = 480 \\text{ minutes}\n  $$\n\n- **This day**:  \n  She **woke up 5 minutes earlier than usual**, so she woke up at:\n  $$\n  6:00 \\text{ a.m.} - 5 \\text{ minutes} = 5:55 \\text{ a.m.}\n  $$\n\n- She was **sleepwalking from 2:15 a.m. to 2:38 a.m.**  \n  That is:\n  $$\n  2:38 \\text{ a.m.} - 2:15 \\text{ a.m.} = 23 \\text{ minutes}\n  $$\n\nNow let's break this down step by step to determine how long **she slept on her bed** that day.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find her **usual sleep window**\nShe usually goes to bed at **10:00 p.m.** and wakes up at **6:00 a.m.**. So **her normal sleep time is from 10:00 p.m. to 6:00 a.m.**\n\n### Step 2: Actual sleep window that day\nShe went to bed at **10:00 p.m.** (same as usual), but woke up **5 minutes early at 5:55 a.m.**\n\nSo **her sleep window that day was**:\n$$\n5:55 \\text{ a.m.} - 10:00 \\text{ p.m.}\n$$\n\nLet\u2019s compute this time difference:\n\n- From **10:00 p.m. to 12:00 a.m.** is **2 hours** = 120 minutes  \n- From **12:00 a.m. to 5:55 a.m.** is **5 hours 55 minutes** = 355 minutes  \n- Total sleep time **before accounting for sleepwalking** =  \n  $$\n  120 + 355 = 475 \\text{ minutes}\n  $$\n\nBut during this time, she **sleepwalked from 2:15 a.m. to 2:38 a.m.**, which is **23 minutes**. So, during those 23 minutes, she was **not on her bed** (she was sleepwalking).\n\nSo the **actual time she was sleeping on her bed** is:\n$$\n475 - 23 = \\boxed{452} \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{452} \\text{ minutes}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 17.043954039923847, "draft_calls": 0, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 139,